    "user_request_original": "Optimize an 18-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45-degree unpolarized incidence. Layer sequence: TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2. Initialize thicknesses from the best prior candidate: [174.84, 198.67, 185.68, 93.00, 163.54, 311.81, 51.85, 93.07, 212.16, 96.65, 172.08, 229.24, 172.56, 90.43, 214.43, 87.04, 206.41, 272.65] nm. Implement two-phase optimization: Phase 1 applies ±10 nm bounds on layers 4-10 (indices 3-9 zero-based) while clamping layers 0-3 and 11-17 to within ±2 nm of initialization. If best_target_score exceeds 0.9200, activate Phase 2 with ±2 nm bounds on all 18 layers. Spectral targets: maximize mean reflectance in 450-650 nm, maximize mean transmittance in 700-1000 nm, suppress transmittance in 450-650 nm and reflectance in 700-1000 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with coherent transfer matrix solver. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize an 18-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica at 45-degree unpolarized incidence using a coherent transfer matrix solver. Initialize thicknesses from the provided sequence. Execute Phase 1 optimization with ±10 nm bounds on layers 4–10 and ±2 nm clamps on remaining layers, then execute Phase 2 with ±2 nm bounds on all 18 layers. Maximize mean reflectance in 450–650 nm and mean transmittance in 700–1000 nm, while minimizing cross-band transmittance and reflectance leakage.",
